  "about": "Capability priors for the KzH adaptive router: the owner's initial observations of what each model family is good at, on the routing dimensions in plugins/jev-router/routing-policy.js. Every number here is evidence, not a routing rule: it seeds a family's profile at the stated confidence and evidence recorded by KzH from real runs, reviews and feedback overtakes it as it accumulates, so an out-of-date score corrects itself. Benchmark evidence comes from the capability benchmark in the Router tab (docs/benchmark.md): a whole run of its small fixed tasks weighs on a dimension as three observations at the benchmark's reliability, so it moves a prior only as far as a few observations can. To edit: give a family a `match` (the providers it runs under and a regular expression over model ids) and one `{ score, confidence, source }` per dimension you have actually observed; leave a dimension out rather than guess, because an absent dimension is reported as unknown at zero confidence and a guessed one is reported as a fact. Add an entry under `models` (keyed by the exact model id) when one version deserves its own numbers; it wins over its family. A model recognised only by its provider inherits the family prior at reduced confidence.",
